        "id": 1121403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-08T20:40:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I put 10 seconds here to begin with as I don\u0027t want this test to be too flaky. \n\nThe SMP_WAIT_FOR_RSP_TIMEOUT_MS in the native stack is actually 30 seconds, but when we are taking more than 10 seconds, there must be some problem. \n\nHowever, if it is more than 1 second, we could fall into the area of Linux context switch delay with Cuttlefish x86 build and so on. \n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/smp/smp_int.h;l\u003d65?q\u003dSMP_WAIT_FOR_RSP_TIMEOUT_MS\n\nNevertheless, since it is all `timeout()` based, successful test runs will not wait for 10 seconds, only failed ones will. 10 seconds give us a better confidence that the failure is real.",
      "parentUuid": "cfc188b4_cc9156c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 75,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "95c08bfebfba40f65dc769490e223e426ce02950",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
