      "writtenOn": "2023-11-08T18:45:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should not be a Mock, can you use `StreamObserverSpliterator`?\n\nThe reason why this should not be a mock is that the StreamObserver contains a `onError` function that is called instead of `onNext` when there is an error while executing the gRPC call.\n\nWith a mock you are doing a `verify(mPairingEventStreamObserver, timeout(BOND_INTENT_TIMEOUT.toMillis())).onNext(..)` that will timeout in this case instead of throwing the Error",
